{"kind":"promise","text":"I will assess my three stale proposals in hugh's ratification queue and record an outcome for each, under planner request 557ed42d.\n\nVERIFIED AT WRITE TIME. 557ed42d is live, unstale, addressed to me, commitment open. All three targets are mine to dispose of: ae78b338 at #319, 0022e9ec at #320, and 9cf51626 at #8998, each unretired and stale.\n\nI NOTE HOW PLANNER FILED THIS, because it is the right shape and worth copying. The three proposals are named in the conditions rather than carried as provenance bases, so this request does not go stale when I retire or supersede them. Filing it the obvious way would have made the request die the moment I acted on it.\n\nWHY THIS IS WORTH DOING FIRST. It is the whole of hugh's ratification queue apart from the genesis roster, and none of it can become a live decision as it stands. That is a queue which looks like it needs a human and cannot use one — the worst state for a row to sit in, and it has been sitting since 2026-08-08 for two of them.\n\nI WILL GIVE A JUDGEMENT ON EACH, not a mechanical re-anchor. Planner asked for one of three outcomes per proposal, and I will say which and why:\n\nae78b338 excludes trust and reputation scoring from gitseq scope, permanently. My first read is that this is still right and still wanted, and that its value is precisely as a standing refusal a future contributor can find — but I will check whether the design-note refusals list already carries the substance, because if it does the proposal is redundant rather than pending.\n\n0022e9ec adopts the intersection rule for promise scope. Its own text says it must not change the fold before the starter definitions land byte-for-byte, so whether it is still adoptable depends on facts about the current vocabulary that I will verify rather than recall.\n\n9cf51626 is composite kinds phase one, adopt submit and defer undertake. It has already been re-anchored once and gone stale again, and it carries describes_superseded_world. Its own argument is that the note is adopted in prose while KindSubmit is absent from the tree — a reader believes a vocabulary the fold will refuse. I will check whether that gap still exists at current main d4f95e37, because if the tree has moved the argument may have been overtaken.\n\nHOW I WILL DECIDE, stated in advance so it is not shaped by what turns out to be least work. Re-anchor and refile only where the proposal would still change what the project does and someone would act on the resulting decision. Retire where the substance has landed or the decision no longer needs making. And say plainly if a proposal was a good idea that nobody is going to implement — a permanently pending decision is worse than a recorded no, because it keeps a human's queue occupied by something that will never move.\n\nI will re-derive each proposal's current bases and the state of what it touches rather than trusting its own text, since all three are stale precisely because the world moved under them. Where I recommend a refile I will do the refile, on current live bases, so hugh gets something ratifiable rather than another assessment.\n\nI will not ratify anything myself: these are mine, and hugh is the ratifier."}